                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "56dacd02-2dcf-376c-a520-563b26077642",
                        "entry_id": "3e759406-ef32-3c40-8574-43a9394edc3d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Serving to commend or compliment; complimentary."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6d9bcb6-52c6-4076-ad75-3fbbeb085180",
                                "sense_id": "56dacd02-2dcf-376c-a520-563b26077642",
                                "text": "1577, Raphael Holinshed et al., The Firste Volume of the Chronicles of England, Scotlande, and Irlande, London: John Hunne, The Historie of England, Kinewulfe, p. 198,\nIn the yeare of our Lorde .786. […] Pope Adrian sent two Lega[ts into] Englande […] with letters commendatory vnto Offa king of Mercia […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cae23072-352d-42a3-bef3-e9a4af38c929",
                                "sense_id": "56dacd02-2dcf-376c-a520-563b26077642",
                                "text": "Pompey had made a Law also, to forbid the custom of making commendatory Orations, on behalf of those that were accused:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fb07607a-6f20-4dfe-aab4-cd9326dc7514",
                                "sense_id": "56dacd02-2dcf-376c-a520-563b26077642",
                                "text": "c. 1726, Alexander Pope, letter to Jonathan Swift dated 8 March, in English Letters and Letter-Writers of the Eighteenth Century, London: George Bell, First Series, 1886, p. 470,\nYou received, I hope, some commendatory verses from a Horse, and a Lilliputian, to Gulliver; and an heroic Epistle to Mrs. Gulliver."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1cc715b6-8331-4c52-a920-3a9e8b65e368",
                                "sense_id": "56dacd02-2dcf-376c-a520-563b26077642",
                                "text": "Some boys had latterly tried to impart gaiety to the ruin by using the central arena as a cricket-ground. But the game usually languished for the aforesaid reason—the dismal privacy which the earthen circle enforced, shutting out every appreciative passer’s vision, every commendatory remark from outsiders—everything, except the sky; and to play at games in such circumstances was like acting to an empty house."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "007e11cf-1170-49aa-82c1-9126940b0976",
                                "sense_id": "56dacd02-2dcf-376c-a520-563b26077642",
                                "text": "One and all, the professors, the preachers, and the editors, hold their jobs by serving the Plutocracy, and their service consists of propagating only such ideas as are either harmless to or commendatory of the Plutocracy."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e82a287d-e620-3fb5-91b2-326c423e3cd5",
                        "entry_id": "3e759406-ef32-3c40-8574-43a9394edc3d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Holding a benefice in commendam."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "831f27f6-addb-4a3d-afe6-d75ea3814163",
                                "sense_id": "e82a287d-e620-3fb5-91b2-326c423e3cd5",
                                "text": "a commendatory bishop"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bf21c092-5281-4de5-8a98-aeb0e0925e83",
                                "sense_id": "e82a287d-e620-3fb5-91b2-326c423e3cd5",
                                "text": "The bishoprics, and the great commendatory abbies, were, with few exceptions, held by that order."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "d395b277-3616-3b78-89b6-13a20ad50aac",
